## 6. Logging

```python
import logging
logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)

# Configure once at startup (structured JSON for production)
logging.basicConfig(
    level=logging.INFO,
    format='{"time":"%(asctime)s","level":"%(levelname)s","logger":"%(name)s","message":"%(message)s"}',
)

# Log with context
logger.info("Product fetched", extra={"sku": sku, "duration_ms": elapsed})
logger.error("Fetch failed", extra={"sku": sku}, exc_info=True)
```

Never use `print()` in production code — logs carry level, timestamp, and source context.

