## 9. What NOT to Do

- Don't use `List`, `Dict`, `Optional`, `Union` from `typing` — use native syntax
- Don't swallow exception context — always `raise X from err`
- Don't use bare `except Exception` — catch specific types
- Don't use `print()` for debugging or logging
- Don't use mutable config — use frozen dataclasses
- Don't use `asyncio.gather` — use `asyncio.TaskGroup` (cancels siblings on failure)
- Don't call sync I/O inside async functions — use `asyncio.to_thread()` for sync wrappers
- Don't use Pydantic v1 API (`class Config:`, `@validator`) — use v2 (`ConfigDict`, `@field_validator`)
